body:
@vvo Adwords retargeting are those ad blocks on websites that display products you recently viewed. To do that Google Adwords needs to know what products a customer viewed/searched for.

To do so we need to implement some code that runs after a search. That code needs to contain this info:

```
<script type="text/javascript">
var google_tag_params = {
ecomm_prodid: "REPLACE_WITH_STRING_VALUE",
ecomm_pagetype: "REPLACE_WITH_STRING_VALUE"
};
</script>
<script type="text/javascript">
/* <![CDATA[ */
var google_conversion_id = xxxxxxxx;
var google_custom_params = window.google_tag_params;
var google_remarketing_only = true;
/* ]]> */
</script>
<script type="text/javascript" src="//www.googleadservices.com/pagead/conversion.js">
</script>
<noscript>
<div style="display:inline;">
<img height="1" width="1" style="border-style:none;" alt="" src="//googleads.g.doubleclick.net/pagead/viewthroughconversion/xxxxxxxx/?value=0&guid=ON&script=0"/>
</div>
</noscript>


```

ecomm\_prodid is an array with the product id's as in the shopping feed
ecomm\_pagetype is a predefined string which is the same for all search queries on this page.

So the main thing is that the ecomm\_prodid gets filled with the product id's after a search and that the listed code is executed.

Is this clear enough? Or do you have additional questions?
